From d21b8bb4062bad39ecc4c27ab8b94513e87be2a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:26:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(quiet): seed registry membership from the process
 reservation; real Registry membership API

Exact-head review 5885418937 (PR #1806) required changes:
1. QuietControl called registry.membership_generation(), which the production
   hermes_cli.local_work.Registry lacked, so every start was refused
   membership_unsupported. Registry now exposes membership_generation(),
   membership_snapshot() and coverage_pending() (membership_unseeded /
   membership_transition_pending). Snapshots with an open membership
   transition are never clean.
2. Nothing seeded membership, so the first reservation latched sticky
   unknown-home. The process reservation (gateway.runtime_ownership
   .process_ownership) is the authority on served homes: it now opens an
   add transition before each gateway.lock acquisition (ready on success,
   removed on failure) and a retire transition around each release. This
   covers the launch home, every multiplex profile and hot-serve add/remove.
   Maintenance owners are separate instances and never touch membership.
   The Registry canonicalizes every home (expanduser/realpath/normcase, as
   hermes_home_key), so symlinked or non-canonical caller spellings match.

Nits: audio _run_reserved releases a still-queued job whose waiter was
cancelled (the job then never runs); _submit_owned releases instead of
latching when a stdlib pool refused a shut-down/broken submit; dispatcher
custody attaches even if the birth fingerprint read raises; a lease-refused
snapshot records the episode as ended; same-boot cooldown uses the elapsed
clock only (a corrected future wall time no longer wedges starts);
run_conversation keeps its own __name__; attestation detects the route
before hashing the interpreter / scanning dependency roots.

Tests drive the production Registry: tests/gateway/test_quiet_membership_seeding.py
(behavioral RED on 95089d00fb: unknown-home after the launch lock) and
test_quiet_control.py now seeds via the tracked ProfileOwnership.
